# Rust / Rune

## Style

- Dense, readable Rust — collapse trivial helpers; keep non-obvious intent in a one-line doc comment
- Prefer `Option` / early return over nested `if`; use `let Some(...) else { return }`
- Name UI element keys stably and uniquely (`"query"`, `"app-{i}"`, `"set-{label}-{name}"`, `"hl-{name}"`) — scroll/focus and tests depend on them
- After button clicks that steal focus, restore `query.focused = true`

## Rune UI

- Build trees with `col` / `row` / `el` / `text` / `text_input` / `spacer`
- Theme via `tok::theme` / `tok::accent`; fonts via `type_::BODY` / `LABEL` / `TITLE`
- Keyboard: handle in `on_input_key` on the search field; Escape and Ctrl+, are reserved
- Grid vs list: Up/Down move by row via `row_step` / `rows` (pins get their own rows); Left/Right only in grid
- Result highlight is one absolutely positioned element; keep `row_h` / `DIVIDER_H` in sync with layout
- App rows: `role("button")` + `on_press_tx` to select and launch; restore `query.focused`
- Icons: `ImageCache` at largest size (48); fallback is a gradient circle + initial

## Desktop entries / launch

```rust
// ❌ BAD — shell out, or whitespace-split Exec
Command::new("sh").args(["-c", &exec])

// ✅ GOOD — exec_args() per the Desktop Entry spec; Command::new(argv[0]).args(&argv[1..]).process_group(0)
// Skip NoDisplay/Hidden/non-Application; trim spaces around `=`; Terminal=true wraps in $TERMINAL / xdg-terminal-exec -e
```

## Tests

- Tests live under `#[cfg(test)]` in the same file; they also run in the Nix sandbox (`nix build`), so no display, no network, no real `$HOME`
- After changes: `cargo clippy --all-targets --locked` clean, and `cargo llvm-cov --locked --fail-under-lines 99.5 --fail-under-regions 99.5`
- Test code meets the same deny lints as app code (no indexing, arithmetic, `as`, `panic!`); only `unwrap`/`expect` are allowed (`clippy.toml`)

### Never touch the user's files

- File paths live in `State.files` (`Files`); app code never builds a config/state path itself
- Tests that save use `temp("name")` and `state(&dir, …)`; tests that don't save use `Path::new(NO_FILES)`
- Take environment values as parameters (`data_dirs(Option<String>)`, `terminal(Option<String>)`, `load_apps(&dirs)`); never `env::set_var` in tests (unsafe in 2024, races between test threads)
- Test apps get `Exec=/nonexistent/<name>` so a launch can't start anything; use `true` for a launch that must succeed

### UI tests

Drive the real view through the headless `rune::Runtime` with the helpers in `mod tests`:

```rust
let mut rt = launcher(state(&dir, &["a", "b"], &[], Settings::default()));
press(&mut rt, Key::Down);          // key into the focused search field
click(&mut rt, "set-Layout-Grid"); // click by element key; settles motion after
assert_eq!(read(&mut rt, |s| s.picked), 1);
```

- `click` must let motion settle: a view still fading in takes no clicks
- Assert behaviour (state, saved files, `rt.find`, `rt.elements()` text), not just that code ran
- `tx.close_window()` is private to rune; a test can run it but can't check it

### Coverage

- `main()` is the only item excluded: `#[cfg_attr(coverage_nightly, coverage(off))]` — it opens a real window
- Don't add `coverage(off)` to tested code, and don't trade an uncoverable exit for indexing with an `#[expect]`
- Every new `?`, `else { return }` or `if let` exit needs a test that takes it, or must be one that can't run
- Known exits that can't run (index lookups from `matches()` / `wrap()`): `flip_pin`, `row_step`, `show_picked`, `results` — keep this list short; prefer code that has no such exit
